# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sampler window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sampler and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-sampler-1 throughout: SB builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after SB's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# SPe (repeat 5 of 5): c2-packed-tp4-diag-sprewarm on the DIAG twin (the old tail, QWEN_FAST_BUDGET_CAP=0; both verify audits OFF; the hang instruments, the
# stall watch at 120 s with its triage and the handle guard in log mode are c2-packed-tp4-diag's). With QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_PREWARM=1: the pinned sampler (the T1 audit's sample_rows call: the sampler all-gather, untilize and ArgMax over 248,320 columns, two 32-row sample_tiles calls for 64 rows) runs ONCE in the packed block's eager warm forward, before the verify capture, and its result is discarded; nothing sampler-related is in the trace or in any replay, and nothing is read back or compared per round.
# Neither arm may change a token: the served path never uses the sampler's output. The factorial's hang shapes, in the order the smoke
# runs them: the engine build after many packed rounds (concurrent4_steady, replay_concurrent4) and the four-user tail
# (concurrent4_v164order, concurrent4). The smoke runs concurrent4 before concurrent4_v164order; the factorial's F1 and F2 skipped
# concurrent4 (v164order, steady, replay only), so a repeat here carries one more four-user job than the factorial's arms did.
# Why: the audits-off hang's factorial (tp4-serve-4, diag profiles, old tail, instruments on): both verify audits on passes; the T1
# audit alone (F1) passes every hang shape; the T2 audit alone (F2) hangs; both off hangs. Every hang is the host blocked in
# ttnn.execute_trace on the FIRST replay of a request's rows=2 verify trace, captured at that request's engine build, after many
# four-user packed rounds. The T1 audit runs the pinned sampler in the packed warm forward and inside the packed capture, and reads
# output[3] back every round. Without it the sampler's state, buffers and programs first come up inside the per-request engine build,
# after the packed capture. These two arms separate the sampler's two placements from the audit's readback and compare.
# Reading: five consecutive runs on the same image, each after its own card reset, that all complete is the evidence this placement
# protects; one stall (the stall watch dumps every thread, runs the triage tools, then ends the process) restarts the count and the
# triage output goes in the report. Two repeats cannot separate a protection from chance at the hang rate seen so far.
# Duration (estimate): 20 min. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sampler-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-diag-sprewarm
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
